    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d681">

                <pb facs="0818" n="808" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg808"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.70/10–444: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-04T15:00:00+01:00">October 4, 1944—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 4—1:29 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8312. For Berle from Allison, Hooker and Moats. ReEmbs 8233, October 2. First
                    meeting with Soviets postponed until 6 p.m., Wednesday, October 4.</p>
                <p>French Delegation to be headed by Massigli<anchor n="43" xml:id="d681-f1"/> or
                    his deputy and to include Jean Levy, former French representative in TACIT.
                    Czech Delegation is headed by Masaryk.<anchor n="44" xml:id="d681-f2"/>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0819" n="809" xml:id="pg809"/>
                <p>Delegation has arrived from Italy including British Colonel from SACMED,<anchor
                        n="45" xml:id="d681-f3"/> American Colonel and civilian from ACC and Italian
                    General who we understand is managing director of Italian State Railways.</p>
                <p>We have been informed that Major General Ross and Lieutenant Colonel Case will
                    attend the Conference and that Ross will be here for the opening meeting and
                    Case will remain through the Conference. [Allison, Hooker, and Moats.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d681-f1" n="43" xml:id="d681-f1-content">
                <p>René Massigli, Minister for Foreign Affairs, French Committee of National
                    Liberation.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d681-f2" n="44" xml:id="d681-f2-content">
                <p>Jan Masaryk, Minister for Foreign Affairs, Czechoslovak Government in Exile.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d681-f3" n="45" xml:id="d681-f3-content">
                <p>Supreme Allied Commander, Mediterranean.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
